.Dd September 30, 2026
.Dt KLDLOAD-TLS-CERT 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm kldload-tls-cert
.Nd keep the web console's TLS certificate valid for every name and address the machine answers on
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -emit
.Nm
.Fl h | -help
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The web console on port 8443, and the terminals and Grafana served
behind it, use one certificate and key,
.Pa /var/lib/kldload/tls/webui.crt
and
.Pa webui.key .
A browser refuses to load one of them inside another when the address in
its bar is not in the certificate, and says nothing about why; so the
certificate has to name every address the machine has, and a new one is
needed whenever an address arrives.
.Pp
.Nm
checks the certificate and writes a new one when:
.Bl -bullet -compact
.It
the certificate or the key is missing;
.It
the certificate expires within a day;
.It
an IPv4 address on a real interface, or a global IPv6 address, is not in
it;
.It
the host name is not in it;
.It
it was not issued by the machine's current authority \(em after
.Ql kldload-ca init --force ,
or a self-signed certificate once the authority exists;
.It
a name or address in
.Pa /etc/kldload/tls-extra-sans.txt
is not in it.
.El
.Pp
Otherwise it does nothing, in a few milliseconds.
.Pp
A new certificate names the full and the short host name,
.Ql localhost ,
.Ql kldload.local ,
127.0.0.1, ::1, 192.168.122.1 (libvirt's network, which may not be up
yet), every address on the machine except the Kubernetes mesh's
.Ql wg-mgmt
and
.Ql wg-k8s ,
and the extra names.
It is issued by the machine's own authority,
.Xr kldload-ca 8 ,
for a year when that authority exists, and is otherwise self-signed for
ten years.
The key is written with mode 0600 in a directory of mode 0700, and the
pair is replaced by renaming, so a reader sees the old pair or the new
one, never half of each; a lock lets only one run work at a time.
After writing, it restarts the services that hold the old certificate
and adds the certificate to the system's trust store.
.Pp
It prints nothing unless
.Fl -emit
is given.
It needs root.
.Pp
It runs from
.Pa kldload-tls-cert.service
at boot once an address is bound, and again on every address change of a
real interface, DHCP renewals included, through NetworkManager's
dispatcher;
.Pa kldload-tls-cert.timer
runs it an hour after its last run if nothing has sooner, which on a DHCP
network is never \(em on a desktop on 2026-09-30 it ran every 30 minutes,
at each lease renewal, and the timer had not fired since boot.
It also runs before
.Xr nginx 8
and the console's proxy start, and whenever the web console starts.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -emit
After the check, print the certificate and then the private key.
.It Fl h , Fl -help
Print the usage and exit 0.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ev KLDLOAD_TLS_CERT_DIR
Where the pair is kept, instead of
.Pa /var/lib/kldload/tls .
.It Ev KLDLOAD_TLS_EXTRA_SANS
The extra-names file, instead of
.Pa /etc/kldload/tls-extra-sans.txt .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa /var/lib/kldload/tls/webui.crt , Pa webui.key
The certificate and key.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/tls-extra-sans.txt
Names and addresses to add, one per line:
.Ql DNS: Ns Ar name ,
.Ql IP: Ns Ar address ,
or either one bare, told apart by its form.
Blank lines and
.Ql #
comments are ignored.
For a name in DNS or an address that is not on any interface of this
machine, such as a floating address in front of it.
.It Pa /etc/kldload/ca/
The authority that issues the certificate.
.It Pa /etc/pki/ca-trust/source/anchors/kldload-webui.crt
The copy in the system trust store, where
.Xr update-ca-trust 8
exists.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Bl -tag -width 1n -compact
.It 0
The certificate is current.
.It 2
A usage error.
.El
.Pp
Any other status is that of the step that failed, which is named on
standard error.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Ss On a kldload desktop
Printed on 2026-09-30.
The certificate was issued by the machine's authority:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# openssl x509 -in /var/lib/kldload/tls/webui.crt -noout -subject -issuer -enddate
subject=CN=webui, O=kldload, OU=kldload services
issuer=CN=kldload-ca kldload-20260830133807-9d6d682dda61b0f5, O=kldload, OU=kldload PKI
notAfter=Sep  8 23:50:19 2027 GMT
.Ed
.Ss From nothing, then adding a name and an address
Printed on 2026-09-30 in a Fedora 44 container named
.Ql demo.example.net ,
with no network and no
.Xr kldload-ca 8 ,
so the certificate is self-signed.
.Xr openssl 1 Ns 's
progress line of dots is left out.
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-tls-cert
-----
# (exited 0)
# ls -l /var/lib/kldload/tls
total 10
-rw------- 1 root root 1314 Sep 30 07:46 webui.crt
-rw------- 1 root root 1704 Sep 30 07:46 webui.key
# openssl x509 -in /var/lib/kldload/tls/webui.crt -noout -subject -issuer -ext subjectAltName
subject=CN=demo.example.net, O=kldload
issuer=CN=demo.example.net, O=kldload
X509v3 Subject Alternative Name:
    DNS:demo.example.net, DNS:demo, DNS:localhost, DNS:kldload.local, IP Address:127.0.0.1, IP Address:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1, IP Address:192.168.122.1
# kldload-tls-cert
# (exited 0)
# cat /etc/kldload/tls-extra-sans.txt
DNS:kvm.example.net
# the VIP
IP:203.0.113.42
# kldload-tls-cert
-----
# (exited 0)
# openssl x509 -in /var/lib/kldload/tls/webui.crt -noout -ext subjectAltName
X509v3 Subject Alternative Name:
    DNS:demo.example.net, DNS:demo, DNS:localhost, DNS:kldload.local, DNS:kvm.example.net, IP Address:127.0.0.1, IP Address:0:0:0:0:0:0:0:1, IP Address:192.168.122.1, IP Address:203.0.113.42
.Ed
.Pp
The second run found nothing to do and printed nothing.
.Ss Printing the pair (--emit)
The same container.
It prints two PEM blocks, the certificate and then the key; the key is not
shown here:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-tls-cert --emit | grep -c -- -----BEGIN
2
# kldload-tls-cert --emit | openssl x509 -noout -subject
subject=CN=demo.example.net, O=kldload
.Ed
.Ss A wrong argument
.Bd -literal -offset indent
# kldload-tls-cert --frob
kldload-tls-cert: unknown argument: --frob (try --help)
# (exited 2)
.Ed
.Sh DIAGNOSTICS
.Bl -diag
.It "kldload-tls-cert: FAIL at line N: command"
A step failed; the command is the one that did.
In a container without
.Xr openssl 1 :
.Bd -literal
/usr/local/sbin/kldload-tls-cert: line 335: openssl: command not found
kldload-tls-cert: FAIL at line 335: openssl req -x509 -nodes -newkey rsa:2048 -keyout "${KEY}.tmp" -out "${CRT}.tmp" -days 3650 -config "${CERT_DIR}/webui.cnf" 1>&2
.Ed
.Pp
It exited 127, the shell's status for a command not found.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr openssl-x509 1 ,
.Xr kldload-ca 8 ,
.Xr kldload-webui 8 ,
.Xr NetworkManager-dispatcher 8 ,
.Xr update-ca-trust 8
.Sh HISTORY
It printed the certificate and the private key on every run, for a
caller that would save them.
No caller did, and
.Xr nginx 8 Ns 's
unit, which meant to discard them with
.Ql >/dev/null ,
had systemd pass that as an argument instead, so the key went into the
journal each time
.Xr nginx 8
started: found on a desktop and on a fresh install on 2026-09-30.
It prints only when asked since, and accepts the literal argument
.Ql >/dev/null ,
doing nothing with it, for units written before.
.Pp
The same day: a new authority from
.Ql kldload-ca init --force
left the console on a certificate signed by the old one, since only names
and expiry were checked; and on a machine without the
.Xr hostname 1
program, every certificate was issued to
.Ql kldload-node ;
it asks the kernel for the name now.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An kldload Aq Mt anthony@kldload.com
.Sh CAVEATS
A key that reached a journal before the change above is still there, and
is the key in use until the certificate is next written.
To replace it now, remove the pair and run
.Nm
again.
.Pp
The trust-store copy is made only where
.Xr update-ca-trust 8
exists, which is the Fedora and Enterprise Linux family.
.Pp
The key is made 0600, but
.Pa kldload-bounce-tls-services ,
which the unit runs next, sets it to 0640, group root, every time; only
the directory's 0700 keeps other users out.
.Pp
Addresses on WireGuard interfaces are not watched: a VPN's address is
added when something else makes a new certificate.
To be sure of it, name it in
.Pa tls-extra-sans.txt .
